4.2 MPC based MCA

The MPC-based MCA, an internal software called ROMA (Renault Optimal Motion-cueing Algorithm), employs a variable time-step algorithm to reduce CPU time. Operating at 200Hz on a Concurrent Real-Time system, it distributes a predictive horizon of about 10s over 50 steps (see Fig. 6). Nominal tilt velocity control is set to 4°/s, but adaptable to 5 or 6°/s under high solicitation and rail acceleration conditions. The threshold of tilt velocity adapted to the rail acceleration level was reported by (Chapron et al. 2007).

