Using all frequency bands signal to make the correlation index can greatly penalize the MCA’s performance with the strategy of multiple scaling factors due to the linear correlation model assuming only one effective scaling factor. Since we have two indices (R% & Rn) obtained by considering all frequency bands' signals and two indices provided by separated LP & HP signals R² & Rc, the correct cues in classification method), the global score is balanced.
For the CTA1 scenario, the LP signal for comparison is filtered using fc=0.10Hz compared to a reference signal filtered by HP fc = 0.15Hz. The HP signal is filtered using fc = 0.45Hz. Other lower cutoff frequencies can also be used.

In the global score estimation, false cues of type 4 are considered the worst, justifying a penalty coefficient three times higher than that of type 2 or 3. The penalty coefficient for false scale cues is set at half the value of the type 2 or 3.

