6.2 Validation with professional drivers
Three professional drivers participated in the MCA performance evaluation. The first driver has experience testing various high-performance driving simulators worldwide. The second driver usually suffers from motion sickness in our previous driving simulator ULTIMATE. The last driver had no prior experience with driving simulators before testing ROADS.
The optimization of MCAs parameters was facilitated by a co-author with expertise in vehicle dynamics mapping.
None of the three professional drivers experienced motion sickness during ROADS driving tests. Although the third driver initially found the car's feeling unnatural compared to a physical car in CTA1 scenario (first driving experience), he quickly adapted to using ROADS to evaluate the performances of various vehicles without issue. Their oral feedback regarding the representativeness of the physical car correlated with the scores presented in this paper.
For the N104 scenario, professional drivers could feel the Renault car's characteristics with MPC-MCA, while only sensing the tendencies of the car's behaviour with CF-MCA, if the tire model or anti-roll bar’s diameter were modified. Regarding the CTA1 scenario, CF-MCA's performance was assessed by driving simulator team and deemed much less performant compared to MPC-MCA. Due to the workload on the ROADS, it is not yet evaluated by the professional driver.
The longitudinal acceleration is also a useful indicator to help the driver to better control the vehicle in high dynamic driving experience (CTA1 scenario). It is tuned to have the best performance below 2m/s².
During the driving experiences, we changed the graphic engine in SCANeR from OSG to Unreal. A significant amelioration has been observed in terms of visual feeling and global feeling by the professional drivers.
7. Conclusion
By using ROADS and MPC-MCA, we have developed a method to assess the high dynamic behaviours on handling track of a passenger car. The method is validated by professional drivers and applicable for vehicle project development.
Thanks to the performance of MPC-MCA in reproducing low frequency motion, the reproduction of high-frequency motion is also improved compared to CF-MCA, thus, increasing the performance of ROADS.

